theorem an-obtain-from-two-sentences
  note        A line of two sentences supplies each apart, so the obtain takes the one that is a "there is".
  let A be a set    (H1)
  let u ∈ A    (H2)
  assume there is x ∈ A with x = u    (H3)
  then there is y ∈ A with y = u

1.  u ∈ A. There is x ∈ A with x = u.
    join H2, H3

2.  x ∈ A. x = u.
    obtain x from line 1

3.  There is y ∈ A with y = u.
    exhibit, from 2
